            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for a small bag, then the French for a rope."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la défaite",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la défaite — \"a defeat\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "défaite is the past participle of the verb for \"to undo\", used as a noun: an undoing. Old French had desfait, \"undone\" (EtymDB 2.1); the verb is built on Latin facere, \"to do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
